 "prompt_sha256": "d0f0903f65716d19e6fa2f5b65ce5dcf112f77e71e0c493d62573732d4b6db03",
 "answer": "To build a vector index over your documents using LlamaIndex, you should use the `VectorStoreIndex` class. This class is designed to handle the creation of an index from a set of documents, enabling efficient retrieval and querying of vectorized representations. \n\nHere's a basic example of how you might use `VectorStoreIndex`:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.core import VectorStoreIndex, SimpleDirectoryReader\n\n# Load documents\ndocuments = SimpleDirectoryReader(\"../../examples/data/paul_graham\").load_data()\n\n# Build the vector index\nindex = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)\n```\n\nIn this example, the documents are loaded using `SimpleDirectoryReader`, and then a vector index is constructed using `VectorStoreIndex.from_documents`. This process involves splitting the documents into chunks and parsing them into nodes, which are then used to create the index.",
